    "tuto.faqTitle": "Frequently asked questions",
    "tuto.ed.title": "Why is video the best way to master AI?",
    "tuto.faq.q1": "Is it legal to watch these videos on your site?",
    "tuto.faq.a1": "Yes, absolutely. We use YouTube's official player and respect the platform's terms of use. The original author keeps all their rights, ads and views. Every view from Albexia counts in the creator's statistics.",
    "tuto.faq.q2": "How are the videos for each tool selected?",
    "tuto.faq.a2": "Our editorial team reviews every submission. We check sound and image quality, but above all educational relevance. A video must bring real added value (tutorial, practical case, comparison) to be approved and appear in our directory.",
    "tuto.faq.q3": "Why filter by duration?",
    "tuto.faq.a3": "Not everyone has the same needs or the same time available. If you just want an overview, a 5-minute video is enough. If you want to set the tool up for your business, you will need 30 to 40 minutes of training. The filter helps you find exactly the content that fits your situation.",
    "tuto.faq.q4": "I'm a YouTuber, why submit my video?",
    "tuto.faq.a4": "Submitting your video puts you in front of a highly targeted audience. A user viewing an AI tool's page is already sold on using it — the ideal place to gain qualified subscribers and build your authority in French-language AI.",
    "tuto.faq.q5": "What happens if a tool changes its interface?",
    "tuto.faq.a5": "That's the advantage of our community-driven system. If a video becomes outdated after an update, the community can flag more recent ones. We regularly refresh tutorials so they match the current versions of the software.",
    "tuto.faq.q6": "Is it free to use the directory and watch the videos?",
    "tuto.faq.a6": "Yes, access to our platform and watching the videos are entirely free. We are funded by affiliate partnerships with the listed tools, so that learning AI stays accessible to everyone, especially in French-speaking countries.",
    "tuto.ed.1": "Video: the ultimate medium for learning technology",
    "tuto.ed.2": "Why did we put video at the heart of our directory? Because in AI, a picture really is worth a thousand words. Reading technical documentation for a new image-generation model like Midjourney or an automation tool like Make can be tedious. By contrast, watching an expert work the interface, adjust prompts and show the mistakes to avoid gives a remarkably steep learning curve.",
    "tuto.ed.3": "Video captures the subtlety of the workflow. It shows real rendering time, interface responsiveness and, above all, the concrete result. By embedding YouTube tutorials directly under our tool pages, we create an immediate learning ecosystem.",
    "tuto.ed.4": "A variety of formats for every need",
    "tuto.ed.5": "We structured our video library to match the diversity of modern usage. Our duration filters give you access to genuine free training: a 40- or 50-minute video is not just a demo, it is a masterclass where the creator takes the time to dig into advanced settings. By filtering videos by duration, we give you back control over your learning time.",
    "tuto.ed.6": "Supporting creators: a win-win relationship",
    "tuto.ed.7": "Our platform rests on a fundamental ethical principle: respecting copyright and supporting content creators. By using the official YouTube player integration, we ensure that every view generated on our directory counts for the original creator. We encourage video authors to submit their own content to strengthen their authority with a qualified audience.",
    // ── Section Écosystème Albexia (accueil) ──
    'eco.title': 'Discover, compare and <span class="text-accent">master</span> AI',
